    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `registrationDate` on owner creation: when the request omits it, it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nThe change threads a single new field through the existing layers, keeping each touched function trivial (no growth of any complex method or large class):\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema. It flows into both the generated request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto` via `allOf`), and MapStruct maps it by name \u2014 so `OwnerMapper` needed no change.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field with a plain getter/setter (one-liners, `@Column(name=\"registration_date\")`).\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the create pipeline's build step now defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when null, preserving a supplied value. This is the sole behavioural change, isolated in the create path (not update).\n- **DB schema** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) so the entity persists consistently.\n- **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 extended the positional seed inserts with a `NULL` for the new column (required so the test HSQLDB context boots).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite are green.",
